ute is a shipping route about 5,600 kilometres (3,500 mi) long. The Northern Sea Route is the shortest shipping route between the western part of Eurasia and the Asia-Pacific region. For China, the NSR can halve the time to Europe compared to via Suez or the Cape of Good Hope routes.","extract_html":"<p>The <b>Northern Sea Route</b> is a shipping route about 5,600 kilometres (3,500 mi) long. The Northern Sea Route is the shortest shipping route between the western part of Eurasia and the Asia-Pacific region. For China, the NSR can halve the time to Europe compared to via Suez or the Cape of Good Hope routes.</p>"}